{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.Stokes3LargeOrderAmplitude","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.Stokes3LargeOrderAmplitude","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Bounds","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Algebra.Order.Field","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Filter.AtTopBot.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Stokes3LargeOrderAmplitude.action_recip_tendsto","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Stokes3LargeOrderAmplitude.action_recip_tendsto","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Stokes3LargeOrderAmplitude.lean#L133-L141","doc":"**Conditional consequence (proved from the carrier).** If the resurgent\naction holds, the reciprocal ratio `κ_{n+1}/(n·κ_n)` converges to `A⁻¹`. This\ninverts the action limit — a genuine derivation of a *new* limit from the class\nfield (not a restatement), so the carrier is non-degenerate (§3b-cond item 5). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Stokes3LargeOrderAmplitude.GeometricKappaAction.action_limit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Stokes3LargeOrderAmplitude.GeometricKappaAction.action_limit","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Stokes3LargeOrderAmplitude.lean#L131-L131","doc":"the action-extraction limit `n·κ_n/κ_{n+1} → A` (numerically `Vol/π`) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Stokes3LargeOrderAmplitude.GeometricKappaAction.hA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Stokes3LargeOrderAmplitude.GeometricKappaAction.hA","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Stokes3LargeOrderAmplitude.lean#L129-L129","doc":"the resurgent action is positive ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Stokes3LargeOrderAmplitude.GeometricKappaAction.kpos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Stokes3LargeOrderAmplitude.GeometricKappaAction.kpos","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Stokes3LargeOrderAmplitude.lean#L127-L127","doc":"the derived Ohtsuki κ-tower is positive ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Stokes3LargeOrderAmplitude.GeometricKappaAction.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Stokes3LargeOrderAmplitude.GeometricKappaAction.mk","kind":"ctor","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Stokes3LargeOrderAmplitude.lean#L125-L125","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Stokes3LargeOrderAmplitude.GeometricKappaAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Stokes3LargeOrderAmplitude.GeometricKappaAction","kind":"class","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Stokes3LargeOrderAmplitude.lean#L113-L131","doc":"**OPEN conjecture-carrier.** The derived `4₁` geometric κ-tower's **action\nlimit** `n·κ_n/κ_{n+1} → A` exists and equals `A` — numerically `A = Vol(4₁)/π`\n(this branch's probe, 12 orders, ~0.3%). Fields:\n\n* `kpos` — the derived positivity of the Ohtsuki κ-tower;\n* `hA` — the action is positive;\n* `action_limit` — the action-extraction limit (the numerically-confirmed but\n  unproved resurgent content).\n\nThe amplitude `= 3` is **deliberately not asserted** (the probe finds it `≈ 1`,\nnot `3`, so the GGM integer stays the state-integral algebraic value). NO\ninstance ⇒ open; the fields are genuine analytic content, not `True`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Stokes3LargeOrderAmplitude.cos_ratio_le_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Stokes3LargeOrderAmplitude.cos_ratio_le_one","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Stokes3LargeOrderAmplitude.lean#L106-L109","doc":"The normalized cosine ratio is bounded by `1` (companion to `cos_envelope`:\n`A_amp` is the tight envelope of the oscillation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Stokes3LargeOrderAmplitude.cos_envelope","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Stokes3LargeOrderAmplitude.cos_envelope","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Stokes3LargeOrderAmplitude.lean#L95-L104","doc":"**Conjugate-pair envelope bound.** A single conjugate-pair contribution\n`A_amp · cos(θ n)` (`A_amp ≥ 0`) never exceeds its envelope `A_amp`. Had the `4₁`\nleading singularity been a genuine `±𝔙` pair, such a term would make the\namplitude oscillate; the 12-order data instead shows a single real singularity\n(monotone `A_n`), so this documents the alternative the probe **ruled out**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Stokes3LargeOrderAmplitude.amplitude_extraction_single","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Stokes3LargeOrderAmplitude.amplitude_extraction_single","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Stokes3LargeOrderAmplitude.lean#L72-L91","doc":"**Amplitude extraction (single singularity).** If a tower factors as\n`κ n = P · g n · (1 + ε n)` with `g n ≠ 0` and subleading corrections `ε n → 0`,\nthen the amplitude functional `κ n / g n` converges to the amplitude `P`. The\nexact statement that the large-order amplitude recovers `P` **when** a single\nBorel singularity governs the growth. ","signatureChunk":0}]}